{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1791143374,"nonce":"UFzwMbyM5kQKAyjwESkN06/JvCM=","target":"c58397869cebe13a90189eb82823f45b08ce14cc618316a9e25c8b322c926a2f","message":"A demo on a par with Blinc's mesh_3d_demo.rs (and later gltf_animation_demo.rs): Khronos' DamagedHelmet, lit by an HDRI, on a grid floor, orbited by drag, zoomed by scroll, panned by shift-drag, with ashui controls over the viewport. It is the 3D half of the canvas epic, b0b7728d2153fa147b757de56303a97bd8f77a131721f571a89008da404a30a9.\n\n- **ashui core**: only what has to touch the renderer. That is depth, the mesh pipeline, environment lighting, and the 3D calls on DrawContext.\n- **ashui-canvaskit**: a side library, after blinc_canvas_kit. It holds cameras, input, the scene kit, primitives, materials and glTF.\n  - It is kept beside `components/` (`canvaskit/haxe/ashui/canvaskit`), with its own classpath.\n  - Core never imports it. It can move to its own repo.\n- Haxe-first throughout:\n  - shaders are hxsl ports of Blinc's `mesh.wgsl`, `skybox.wgsl`, `shadow.wgsl` and the kit's `grid.wgsl`;\n  - no new natives unless a decoder is unavoidable.\n- hlwgpu already has depth-stencil attachments, cube textures and compute.\n\n1. **Math**: Vec3, Vec4, Quat and Mat4 in `ashui.math`:\n   - perspective, lookAt, inverse and normal matrix;\n   - ash-simd for bulk work (joint palettes), with a plain fallback on stock HL.\n2. **Layer mode with depth** (step 4 of the hand-off): the canvas renders into its own colour and depth texture at on-screen size, and the placeholder record composites it like an image. The canvas's clips, fades and opacity therefore still apply.\n3. **DrawContext 3D**: `setCamera`, `drawMesh(mesh, transform)`, `setLights` and `setEnvironment`.\n   - Types: MeshData (vertices, indices and material), Vertex (position, normal, uv, colour, tangent, joints, weights), Material (metallic-roughness PBR) and Light (directional, point, spot).\n   - A mesh's GPU buffers and textures are uploaded once, cached by identity and freed with it. The CPU copies are dropped after upload.\n4. **MeshShader (hxsl)**, built up in stages:\n   - unlit, then Lambert, then GGX PBR;\n   - textures: base colour, normal map, metal-rough, emissive and occlusion;\n   - alpha modes: opaque, mask and blend (blend sorted back to front).\n5. **Environment**:\n   - Radiance `.hdr` (RGBE) decoded in Haxe;\n   - equirect to cubemap, an irradiance map, a prefiltered specular map and a BRDF LUT, in compute passes;\n   - a skybox pass.\n6. **Shadows**: a directional shadow map with PCF.\n7. **Later**: skinning and morph targets (joint matrices and morph deltas in storage buffers), as the drone demo needs.\n\n- **OrbitCamera**: target, distance, azimuth, elevation and fov; `orbit`, `zoom`, `pan`.\n  - It is a signal, so the canvas redraws only when the camera moves (Solid style, no per-frame rebuild).\n- **Input** on the canvas element:\n  - drag orbits; shift-drag or middle-drag pans; scroll and pinch zoom;\n  - momentum with decay, run by AnimationScheduler, so it stops when settled and is deterministic in recordings;\n  - nothing ticks while the canvas is out of view (`inView`).\n- **SceneKit3D**:\n  - a camera, a light rig, an environment, `withHdri`, `withGrid`;\n  - a mesh registry with handles (setPosition, setRotation, setScale, setVisible);\n  - `element(render)` returns the `\u003ccanvas\u003e`;\n  - a loading state while assets decode on an Ash fiber (`ash.Future`), synchronous on stock HL.\n- **Grid pass**: an infinite floor grid that fades with distance.\n- **Geometry and materials**:\n  - primitives: plane, cube, sphere, cylinder and torus;\n  - a material builder (material.rs).\n- **glTF 2.0 loader** in Haxe:\n  - `.gltf` + `.bin` and `.glb`; meshes, materials, textures and the node tree;\n  - animations later, with skinning.\n- **The 2D side, later**: CanvasKit's pan/zoom viewport, background patterns, selection, snapping and the spatial index. Moving Painter and Sketch here is a separate decision.\n\n- The helmet on the grid under the HDRI, with orbit, pan and zoom.\n- A side panel of ashui components:\n  - exposure, light intensity and direction;\n  - toggles for grid, skybox and shadows;\n  - an environment picker;\n  - a reset-camera button.\n- A loading overlay that leaves when the scene is ready.\n- Assets copied from Blinc's `examples/assets/3d` with their licence files: DamagedHelmet (CC BY-NC, credit as Blinc gives it) and `rogland_clear_night_2k.hdr`.\n\n- Unit tests:\n  - Mat4 and Quat math, and the camera's eye and orbit;\n  - glTF parsing of a minimal fixture (Khronos Box), and HDR decoding of a tiny fixture.\n- Pixel tests:\n  - depth ordering of two overlapping cubes;\n  - lit faces of a cube shaded by light direction;\n  - a 3D canvas still clipped by a rounded parent.\n- A snapshot scene of the helmet, and a MotionRecorder run of orbit momentum settling.\n- Memory and CPU checks:\n  - idle at rest (no redraw without a camera or scene change);\n  - steady memory after load, compared against Blinc's demo.\n\nmath, then layer mode with depth, then the mesh pipeline (unlit → PBR), then the kit (camera, input, grid, primitives), then the demo on primitives, then glTF and the helmet, then HDR, IBL and skybox, then shadows, then skinning and animation.","files":null}]}